  "name": "minishogi",
  "description": "Minishogi, shogi on a 5x5 board, devised around 1970 by Shigenobu Kusumoto of Osaka. Each side has a king, a gold, a silver, a bishop, a rook and one pawn; captured pieces change sides and may be dropped back. Every piece but the king and the gold promotes on the far rank, the pawn always. A pawn may not be dropped on a file already holding one of its side's pawns, nor to give mate. One departure: a fourth repetition is a draw here, where the published rule makes it a loss for the first player (for the checking side under perpetual check).",
